Crop production under the nuclear-winter scenarios (data/drivers/crops_*Tg.npz)
  Crop-model simulations of Blouin et al. (2025), no crop relocation.

Pasture production and climate of the scenarios (data/drivers/grass_*Tg.csv, data/cold_deficit.npz,
data/decay_temperature.npz)
  Derived from the climate and pasture simulations of Xia, L., et al. (2022). Global food insecurity and
  famine from reduced crop, marine fishery and livestock production due to climate disruption from nuclear
  war soot injection. Nature Food 3, 586-596. https://doi.org/10.1038/s43016-022-00573-0. Data at
  https://osf.io/yrbse/. Country-level ratios and monthly means only.

MapSPAM 2020 (data/crop_yield.csv, data/residue_access.csv, data/residue_access_crops.npz,
data/residue_calendar.csv, data/map_context/maps_05deg.npz)
  International Food Policy Research Institute (IFPRI). 2024. Global Spatially-Disaggregated Crop Production
  Statistics Data for 2020 Version 1.0.0. https://doi.org/10.7910/DVN/SWPENT. Harvard Dataverse. Version 3.
  CC BY 4.0.
  This data was provided by the International Food Policy Research Institute (IFPRI). IFPRI bears no
  responsibility for the analyses or interpretations of the data presented here.

FAOSTAT (data/drivers/animal_baseline.csv, data/ruminant_herds.csv, data/grain_feed.csv)
  FAO. 2025. FAOSTAT: Crops and livestock products. Accessed on 23 December 2025.
  FAO. 2026. FAOSTAT: Food Balances. Accessed on 9 November 2026.
  https://www.fao.org/faostat/en/#data. Licence: CC-BY-4.0. FAO does not endorse this work.

Gridded Livestock of the World (data/grass_climate.csv, data/cold_deficit.npz, data/residue_access.csv, data/residue_access_crops.npz, data/map_context/maps_05deg.npz)
  FAO. 2024. Gridded livestock density (Global - 2020 - 10 km), GLW4.
  https://data.apps.fao.org/catalog/dataset/9d1e149b-d63f-4213-978b-317a8eb42d02. CC BY 4.0. FAO does not
  endorse this work.

Cereal residue production and uses (data/benchmark_smerald.csv, data/residue_reserve.csv,
results/residue_benchmark.csv)
  Smerald, A. (2023). Global crop residue management dataset (1997-2021). Karlsruhe Institute of Technology.
  https://doi.org/10.35097/989. CC BY 4.0. Values averaged over 2019 to 2021; regional shares aggregated by
  the authors.

Feed values (data/residue_feed_values.csv, data/stream_properties.csv, data/protein_streams.csv,
data/protein_residues.csv)
  Metabolizable energy, crude protein, NDF and protein degradability are taken or derived from Feedipedia, a
  programme by INRAE, CIRAD, AFZ and FAO (https://www.feedipedia.org), acknowledged as source and copyright
  holder. Feedipedia allows extracts for research and non-commercial use; these values are not licensed under
  the Apache License 2.0.

Rations (data/stream_properties.csv)
  Dry-matter shares of the rations derived from Mottet, A., et al. (2017). Livestock: On our plates or eating
  at our table? A new analysis of the feed/food debate. Global Food Security 14, 1-8, Supplementary
  Information 4 to 9, aggregated to six herds by the authors.

Crop calendars (data/residue_calendar.csv, data/residue_clearing.npz)
  Harvest and planting timing derived from the crop calendar dataset of Sacks, W.J., et al. (2010). Crop
  planting dates: an analysis of global patterns. Global Ecology and Biogeography 19, 607-620.

Present climate (data/grass_climate.csv)
  The share of each herd in a temperate climate is computed from WorldClim 2.1 (Fick and Hijmans, 2017). No WorldClim data are redistributed.

Population (data/population.csv)
  United Nations, Department of Economic and Social Affairs, Population Division (2024). World Population
  Prospects 2024, Online Edition. CC BY 3.0 IGO.

Country boundaries (data/map_context/countries.geojson)
  Made with Natural Earth (public domain), simplified for plotting.

United States Department of Agriculture (data/grain_feed.csv, data/stream_properties.csv,
data/residue_decay_crops.csv)
  Production, Supply and Distribution database; FoodData Central; RUSLE2 science documentation (2013). Public
  domain.

Individual coefficients from the literature (NRC, IPCC and the papers cited in the paper's Methods and
Supplementary Material) are given with their source in the code and data files.
